Rules You
Must Know
Everything is public before registration opens, so you can read exactly how you will be judged and then decide. These nine are the ones that decide whether your night goes well.

Teams of 2 to 4, and everyone signs for themselves
You bring your own team and register as a complete team. Every team is scored the same way, regardless of size, and we do not match individuals into teams. The Team Leader will submit the team’s verification video through the application survey, while each member agrees to the terms using their own email. The Team Leader cannot accept the terms on behalf of any other team member.

All AI tools are allowed
Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Copilot, anything you like. No limits and nothing to declare. We want to see how well you direct them, because that is how the work is actually done now.

Your setup is your responsibility
Internet, electricity, laptop, camera and microphone. All of it is on you. You are asked for your backup plan at registration because we expect you to have one: a second connection, a charged power bank, and everything tested before the day.

A dead connection does not stop the clock
If you drop, the four hours keep running. No restart, no extra time, no re-run. Post in your team channel when you are back so there is a record. The only exception is an area wide outage that takes your whole team offline at once, and that is judged by the event lead on the night.

Camera on, and a proctor is in the room
A proctor is in your room for the full four hours, and there are four formal checks announced in your channel before each one. A blurred background is fine. What the proctor writes down is also where internship offers come from, so this is not only about catching cheating.

Everything runs through your team channel
Once your team is confirmed you get a private Discord channel with your proctor in it. Camera checks, outage reports, questions and your submission links all go there. The server is for confirmed teams only.

Host it anywhere, but it must open at 10:00 PM
Vercel, Netlify, Render, Cloudflare, your own server. We health check and screenshot every URL once at the close, and that capture is what gets judged. If your host sleeps free instances or your deploy breaks at 9:55, that is on you.

Your speed bonus comes from your last commit
Keep building and your score goes up while the speed bonus comes down. Stop early and you keep the bonus. Your call, and the same rule for everyone. The bonus is zero unless 3 of the 4 requirements work on both problems.

Open source is fine, with two limits
No AGPL, GPL or SSPL, and nothing marked non-commercial. MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD and ISC are all fine. You send a short LICENSES.md with what you used.

